  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">STFA Joint Programme for the Northern Region of Afghanistan: Addressing Basic Human Needs through the ABADEI Strategy  - Outcome 3 Disaster and climate resilient critical infrastructure</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In partnership with Save the Children, IOM will contribute to the overall objective of supporting the people of Afghanistan to live in safety and with dignity through greater economic stability and increased ability to meet acute and immediate needs. This will be done through two areas of intervention: 1) Cash component &#x2013; building off of on-going cash programming, Save the Children will reach an estimated 4,600 persons with multi-purpose cash assistance, to be utilized for meeting a range of immediate needs, including: shelter repair and non-food items; winterization support including heating/fuel; food and water security/nutrition, transportation, clothing and healthcare/medicines, education, etc.; 2) Emergency livelihoods -IOM will provide temporary jobs to 1,800 individuals in order to offer immediate access to income for at-risk community members predominantly through cash-for-work interventions; as well as support to 250 businesses (across 6 districts and 60 communities) vulnerable to the evolving context, through the replacement of critical and necessary productive assets, thus safeguarding and re-instating the livelihoods of employees and business owners.</narrative>
  </description>
